  * Development series after the 0.1.2 release.

 -- Geoff Hackett <ghackett@episode6.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:45:45 -0400

collins (0.1.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Collins is on Fedora: the episode6/stable COPR builds every release for
    every current Fedora and for RHEL 10 and its rebuilds; the RPM carries
    the same GTK 4.10 / libadwaita 1.5 floors as the .deb.
  * Notification sound plays through GStreamer (gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0 and
    gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0, new Recommends); five CC0 chimes ship with
    the app.
  * In-app notifications: a session that speaks up from a tab you aren't
    looking at shows a card in the window and plays a sound while Collins
    is focused (the desktop notification now covers the times it isn't); a
    header bell wears the unread count and opens a notification history
    sheet (Ctrl+Shift+B); a Notifications preferences group holds the
    switches, the Sound picker (desktop theme sounds, bundled chimes, or a
    file), a Card theme row pinning the card light or dark, and Announce
    finished runs.
  * Collins checks GitHub once a day for a newer release and says so with a
    notification; Check for updates in Preferences → General turns it off.
  * New sessions open onto a new-chat screen with model and effort pickers
    (pre-selecting the CLI's defaults) and a worktree checkbox; an unsent
    screen is kept as a sidebar Draft row; an empty send launches an empty
    session; the Advanced new-session dialog is gone.
  * An effort picker rides beside the model picker (composer and new-chat
    screen), the footer's model chip shows the level, and /effort follows
    a pick on a running session; session titles are generated at low
    effort.
  * Token use: a preferences group gathers everything that runs Claude on
    your behalf (with a login auto-renew switch), a first-launch dialog
    discloses it, the headless runs pass --strict-mcp-config --tools "",
    and the title/icon model pickers gain a None option; an expired Claude
    login repairs itself with a throwaway claude -p, backing off
    exponentially.
  * Composer: paste an image from the clipboard; a big draft survives the
    close/reopen round trip (typed back in pieces the CLI shows in full);
    every way in appends at the end of the box.
  * The editor shows one column at a time when its column is 500 px or
    narrower; a back button beside the tabs returns to the file tree.
  * The status icon's drink turns into the sidebar's blue barber pole while
    any session is working, and back to the coral pour when the last run
    stops.
  * PR page: refreshes patch the page in place instead of rebuilding it;
    the Checks list folds past four rows behind "Show more"; a draft's
    Ready button offers mark-ready-and-merge on right-click; right-clicking
    the Conversation or Files tab opens that view on github.com; the folded
    description shows the start of its first paragraph; the description no
    longer selects itself after a background re-read; a page opened in a
    background tab gets its full width.
  * Project rows: clicking a header starts a session there (the icon strip
    folds the group); the right-click menu gains Checkout main; headers
    are centred in their rows.
  * The session tab bar under the header is hidden by default; the
    header's toggle shows it, and a window that had it showing keeps it.
  * Bringing Collins back from the tray no longer leaves GNOME's busy
    cursor up: the window is raised on the host's activation token.
  * Labels no longer select all their text when the keyboard reaches them
    without a click: GTK's select-on-focus is off across the app.

 -- Geoff Hackett <ghackett@episode6.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:45:45 -0400

collins (0.1.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Collins is now published to ppa:episode6/stable, for Ubuntu 24.04 (noble)
    and 26.04 (resolute).
  * Install alongside agent-session-manager instead of colliding with it: the
    action icons move out of the shared hicolor theme into
    /usr/share/collins/icons, which both packages claimed copies of
    (agent-claude-symbolic.svg and tab-close-symbolic.svg).
  * Require libadwaita 1.5 and GTK 4.10 explicitly, so a distribution too old
    to run Collins refuses the package instead of installing it and failing at
    launch.
  * libspelling is optional now (Depends -> Recommends): without it the
    prompt composer is a plain text box instead of refusing to launch the
    app.
  * Every keyboard shortcut is rebindable from a Keyboard Bindings dialog in
    the sidebar menu; Ctrl+K is the quick switcher, Ctrl+Shift+K clears the
    terminal panel, and Ctrl+Shift+F no longer opens the sidebar search.
  * Close can hide the window and keep every session running; the status
    icon, a notification, or relaunching brings it back.
  * Collins is on PyPI as plain "collins", and the sidebar menu offers the
    Ubuntu PPA to an install that didn't come from it.
  * Session tools: start_session takes a model, and a spawned sibling
    inherits the caller's model and permission mode.
  * Generate Icon picks its model per run; the model list is cached for a
    day and across restarts, with a Refresh row in Preferences, and the
    pickers group it by family.
  * The project row's menu pulls its branch; the composer opens on typing by
    default and never loses a draft; its spell-check menu aims at the word
    you clicked.
  * PR pages open wider when the gutter is free, render changed images as
    images, and follow running checks with free conditional requests instead
    of waiting for the next minute.
  * Ctrl+click finishes a wrapped link from the transcript when the screen
    can't.
  * Preferences regrouped into ten groups; notifications withdraw themselves
    when what they say stops being true.
  * Fixes: archiving clears a session's notification and unread count; the
    status icon's menu no longer draws "Quit" on a separator; a click in the
    gutter beside a width-limited terminal focuses it and clears unread.

 -- Geoff Hackett <ghackett@episode6.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:21:01 -0400

